# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Job splitting {#job-splitting}"
msgstr "Pembagian job {#job-splitting}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When you have to split one job into several because mixed shot or precision\n"
"values in a single job are no longer supported, consider the following:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ketika kamu harus membagi satu job menjadi beberapa job karena nilai shot atau precision\n"
"campuran dalam satu job tidak lagi didukung, pertimbangkan hal berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Group the PUBs by their target value — one job per distinct value, not one job per\n"
"PUB.** Splitting is a regrouping, so the total number of PUBs you submit does not change.\n"
"For example, given `[A@0.01, B@0.05, C@0.01]`, submit two jobs: `[A, C]` at `precision=0.01` and `[B]`\n"
"at `precision=0.05`. Submitting `A` and `C` as separate jobs is less efficient, as each job comes with a fixed overhead.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kelompokkan PUB berdasarkan nilai targetnya — satu job per nilai yang berbeda, bukan satu job per\n"
"PUB.** Pembagian adalah pengelompokan ulang, sehingga jumlah total PUB yang kamu kirim tidak berubah.\n"
"Sebagai contoh, dengan `[A@0.01, B@0.05, C@0.01]`, kirim dua job: `[A, C]` pada `precision=0.01` dan `[B]`\n"
"pada `precision=0.05`. Mengirim `A` dan `C` sebagai job terpisah kurang efisien, karena setiap job memiliki overhead tetap.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Learn once and use the noise models in all split jobs.** It is more efficient to\n"
"run a single `NoiseLearnerV3` job over the union of all layers.\n"
"The result of a noise learner job contains a list of `NoiseLearnerV3Result` objects,\n"
"one for each input instruction, and is in the same order as the input list. You can\n"
"use the output of this noise learner job in all the split (Estimator) jobs, and noise\n"
"models for layers not in the PUBs of a split job are ignored.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pelajari sekali dan gunakan model noise di semua job hasil pembagian.** Lebih efisien untuk\n"
"menjalankan satu job `NoiseLearnerV3` atas gabungan semua layer.\n"
"Hasil dari job noise learner berisi daftar objek `NoiseLearnerV3Result`,\n"
"satu untuk setiap instruksi input, dan berada dalam urutan yang sama dengan daftar input. Kamu bisa\n"
"menggunakan output dari job noise learner ini di semua job (Estimator) hasil pembagian, dan model\n"
"noise untuk layer yang tidak ada di PUB job hasil pembagian akan diabaikan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Submit all the split jobs in a `Batch` first, then collect their results.**\n"
"The `Batch` execution mode provides efficient parallel execution when there are multiple jobs.\n"
"However, `job.result()` is blocking, so calling it inside the submission loop serializes the jobs and negates the benefits of using `Batch`.\n"
"Make sure you use the submit-all-then-collect pattern (shown below).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kirim semua job hasil pembagian dalam `Batch` terlebih dahulu, lalu kumpulkan hasilnya.**\n"
"Mode eksekusi `Batch` menyediakan eksekusi paralel yang efisien ketika ada banyak job.\n"
"Namun, `job.result()` bersifat blocking, sehingga memanggilnya di dalam loop pengiriman akan menyerialisasi job dan menghilangkan manfaat penggunaan `Batch`.\n"
"Pastikan kamu menggunakan pola kirim-semua-lalu-kumpulkan (ditunjukkan di bawah).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the following example, `pub1` and `pub2` require `precision=0.5`, whereas `pub3` requires `precision=0.1`:\n"
msgstr "Dalam contoh berikut, `pub1` dan `pub2` memerlukan `precision=0.5`, sedangkan `pub3` memerlukan `precision=0.1`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
